 "agentCfg.key.GIO_ADVERTISED_HOST.sub": "A host name the agent looks up and follows, re-advertising the new address when it changes — for a home connection with a dynamic IP. Set this or a public IP, not both.",
 "agentCfg.key.GIO_ADVERTISED_IP": "Public IP (advertised)",
 "agentCfg.key.GIO_ADVERTISED_IP.help": "The PUBLIC (internet) IP that players outside the server's network connect to. Behind a router (the server only has a private address such as 192.168.x.x): put the router's public IP here and forward TCP 21000, UDP 21081 and the agent's TCP port (18080 unless you changed it) to the server — players on the server's own network then need NAT loopback on the router. Empty = the bind IP is advertised: right for a server whose own address is public (a VPS), LAN-only behind a router. An IP that changes? Use the DDNS host name instead.",
 "agentCfg.key.GIO_ADVERTISED_IP.sub": "The address game clients are told to connect to. Empty = the stack's own local IP (fine on a LAN). Set this or a DNS name below, not both.",
 "agentCfg.key.GIO_BIND_IP": "Local bind IP",
 "agentCfg.key.GIO_BIND_IP.sub": "The local address docker publishes the game ports on (the stack's .env OUTER_IP). Empty = the machine's primary IP. Used when a server version is first prepared (or repaired from a loopback setup); an installed version keeps the address it was set up with. Not applied while “Keep .env settings” is on.",
 "agentCfg.key.GIO_CA_FILE": "Extra trusted root certificates",
 "agentCfg.key.GIO_CA_FILE.sub": "Full path of a PEM file with more root certificates to trust on top of the system's (corporate TLS inspection, an antivirus web shield). Empty = the system store only.",
 "agentCfg.key.GIO_FETCH_DISK_RESERVE": "Free space kept by server downloads",
 "agentCfg.key.GIO_FETCH_DISK_RESERVE.sub": "A server package download does not start unless this much stays free on that drive after the archive and the unpacked files — docker images and the database need room right after it.",
 "agentCfg.key.GIO_HOTPATCH_BUNDLES": "Use the archive.org bundles",
 "agentCfg.key.GIO_HOTPATCH_BUNDLES.sub": "Off = never download the ready-made bundles, whatever the hotpatch card's Mirror source says; every file then comes from the official CDN.",
 "agentCfg.key.GIO_HOTPATCH_BUNDLE_DIR": "Hotpatch bundle folder",
 "agentCfg.key.GIO_HOTPATCH_BUNDLE_DIR.sub": "Where the archive.org bundles are downloaded and unpacked before their files join the mirror. Must be outside the mirror folder, and not a drive root, a server folder or one of the agent's own folders. Empty = hotpatch-bundles beside the mirror.",
 "agentCfg.key.GIO_HOTPATCH_DIR": "Hotpatch mirror folder",
 "agentCfg.key.GIO_HOTPATCH_DIR.sub": "Where the mirrored fixes and voice packs are kept. Everything in this folder is served to anyone who can reach the agent, without a token — give it a folder of its own that holds nothing but the mirror (a drive root, a server folder or one of the agent's own folders is refused). Empty = beside the agent's state file. Existing files are NOT moved: move them yourself before the restart, or the mirror starts empty.",
 "agentCfg.key.GIO_HOTPATCH_DISK_RESERVE": "Free space kept by voice-pack downloads",
 "agentCfg.key.GIO_HOTPATCH_DISK_RESERVE.sub": "Mirroring voice packs (3–9 GB per language) does not start if it would leave less than this free on the mirror's drive — a full disk takes the database down with it.",
 "agentCfg.key.GIO_HOTPATCH_ONDEMAND_MAX": "On-demand download budget",
