 "server.adv.flaskVendorKept": "Flask secret: vendor default — kept as it is: this agent keeps .env settings (change it under Server secrets)",
 "server.adv.hint": "\"Re-apply the GAA progress\" opens the same choice as \"Prepare the server\": importing the default save puts the starting progress back, so it DELETES everything people have played since (and stops the server while it works, so it kicks the players out of the game); keeping your own progress or applying the fixes only touches no save. \"Re-apply the events\" only reopens the GAA events, closes the others and refreshes the Spiral Abyss calendar — the save is NOT touched, nobody loses anything; it works only while the server is running, because at every start all of this is applied on its own anyway. The txt fixes are usually applied together with the save, when the server is prepared — from here you remove them (or add them later) if they turn out to break chapter 1 of the GAA quest. The public address is re-applied if the server moved to another IP. \"Copy account progress\" duplicates one account's save onto another account (new or existing) — the server stays up, only the two players must be logged out of the game.",
